---

<StandardPageLayout
  code='ASBE No. 06'
  standardType='ASBE'
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued='2006-02'
  latestAmendment='2017-01'
  status='Active'
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope and Recognition Criteria" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Land Use Rights as Intangible Assets" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Initial Measurement â€” At Cost" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Internally Generated Intangibles â€” the Research/Development Split" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Development-Phase Capitalisation Criteria" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Subsequent Measurement â€” Amortisation and the No-Revaluation Rule" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Finite vs Indefinite Useful Life" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example â€” Capitalising Development Costs" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example â€” Amortising a Land Use Right" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IAS 38" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Identifiable non-monetary assets without physical substance</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 6 governs IDENTIFIABLE non-monetary ASSETS WITHOUT physical SUBSTANCE â€” patents, TRADEMARKS, copyrights, and (GENUINELY distinctively) LAND USE RIGHTS held for the enterprise's OWN operational USE. The Standard is BROADLY converged with IAS 38 internationally, INCLUDING the SAME research/development CAPITALISATION split, though it SHARES the SAME cost-model-ONLY restriction seen ELSEWHERE across the ASBE ASSET standards.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope and Recognition Criteria</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Identifiability, control, and probable future economic benefit</div><div class="principle">An INTANGIBLE asset is RECOGNISED where it is IDENTIFIABLE (SEPARABLE, or ARISING from CONTRACTUAL/legal RIGHTS), CONTROLLED by the ENTERPRISE, and EXPECTED to GENERATE probable FUTURE economic BENEFITS, WITH its cost MEASURABLE reliably.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Land Use Rights as Intangible Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A genuinely distinctive classification reflecting China's land system</div><div class="principle">GIVEN China's STATE (or COLLECTIVE) land OWNERSHIP system, enterprises HOLD "LAND USE RIGHTS" â€” a CONTRACTUAL right to USE land for a DEFINED period â€” RATHER than FREEHOLD land OWNERSHIP. WHERE such RIGHTS are held for the enterprise's OWN operational USE (as OPPOSED to leasing OUT or capital APPRECIATION, which would FALL under ASBE No. 3, Investment Property), they are CLASSIFIED as INTANGIBLE assets under THIS Standard â€” a GENUINELY distinctive CLASSIFICATION without a DIRECT IFRS/US GAAP PARALLEL, since NEITHER framework has an EQUIVALENT land-TENURE construct of the SAME type.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Initial Measurement â€” At Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Purchase price plus directly attributable costs</div><div class="principle">An INTANGIBLE asset ACQUIRED separately is MEASURED at COST â€” the PURCHASE price PLUS directly ATTRIBUTABLE costs of PREPARING the asset for its INTENDED use. INTANGIBLE assets ACQUIRED WITHIN a business COMBINATION are measured at FAIR VALUE at the ACQUISITION date (UNLESS the combination is UNDER common CONTROL â€” see the COMPANION ASBE No. 2 poster).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Internally Generated Intangibles â€” the Research/Development Split</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Research expensed, development capitalised if criteria are met</div><div class="principle">EXPENDITURE incurred DURING the RESEARCH phase (ORIGINAL, planned INVESTIGATION undertaken with the PROSPECT of gaining NEW scientific or TECHNICAL knowledge) is EXPENSED as INCURRED â€” the enterprise CANNOT yet DEMONSTRATE that a FUTURE economic BENEFIT will FLOW. EXPENDITURE incurred DURING the DEVELOPMENT phase (APPLYING research FINDINGS to a PLAN for producing NEW or SUBSTANTIALLY improved PRODUCTS or processes) MAY be CAPITALISED, but ONLY if SPECIFIC criteria are MET (Section 6) â€” a SPLIT CONVERGED with IAS 38's OWN research/development DISTINCTION internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Development-Phase Capitalisation Criteria</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All conditions must be demonstrated</div><div class="check-list"><span>Technical feasibility of completing the intangible asset for use or sale</span><span>Intention to complete the intangible asset and use or sell it</span><span>Ability to use or sell the intangible asset</span><span>How the intangible asset will generate probable future economic benefits</span><span>Availability of adequate resources to complete development</span><span>Ability to measure the development expenditure reliably</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Subsequent Measurement â€” Amortisation and the No-Revaluation Rule</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cost model only, consistent with fixed assets</div><div class="principle">CONSISTENT with the SAME cost-model-ONLY restriction seen for FIXED assets (ASBE No. 4), NO revaluation MODEL is available for INTANGIBLE assets under ASBE No. 6 â€” they are CARRIED at COST less ACCUMULATED amortisation (for FINITE-life intangibles) and IMPAIRMENT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Finite vs Indefinite Useful Life</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Amortisation only for finite-life intangibles</div><div class="principle">Intangible ASSETS with a FINITE useful LIFE are AMORTISED systematically OVER that LIFE. Intangible ASSETS with an INDEFINITE useful LIFE (WHERE there is NO foreseeable LIMIT to the PERIOD over WHICH the asset is EXPECTED to GENERATE benefits) are NOT amortised, but are TESTED for IMPAIRMENT ANNUALLY â€” CONSISTENT with IAS 38's OWN approach internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example â€” Capitalising Development Costs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Splitting research and development expenditure</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A new product development project</div><div class="wk-body">A company spends RMB 3,000,000 on early-stage research into a new technology (technical feasibility not yet established), and a further RMB 5,000,000 on subsequent development after feasibility, intent, and resources are all clearly demonstrated.</div><div class="wk-answer">The RMB 3,000,000 RESEARCH cost is <strong>EXPENSED</strong> as incurred. The RMB 5,000,000 DEVELOPMENT cost is <strong>CAPITALISED</strong> as an intangible asset, since ALL the development-phase CRITERIA (Section 6) are DEMONSTRATED â€” to be AMORTISED over its USEFUL life once the asset is READY for its intended USE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example â€” Amortising a Land Use Right</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A distinctively Chinese intangible asset</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A 50-year land use right for a factory site</div><div class="wk-body">A company acquires a land use right for its own factory site, at a cost of RMB 40,000,000, for a defined term of 50 years.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises an INTANGIBLE ASSET of RMB 40,000,000, AMORTISED on a straight-line BASIS over the 50-year TERM: RMB 40,000,000 Ã· 50 = <strong>RMB 800,000 per year</strong> â€” a GENUINELY distinctive CLASSIFICATION reflecting China's land TENURE system.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 6 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Useful lives (finite or indefinite), and amortisation methods, by class of intangible asset</span><span>Research and development expenditure recognised as an expense during the period</span><span>Carrying amount of intangible assets with restricted title or pledged as security</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Determining the point at which a project moves from research to development</span><span>Whether an intangible asset has a finite or indefinite useful life</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Useful life and amortisation method for finite-life intangibles</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 38</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison â€” ASBE 6 vs IAS 38</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 6</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 38</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Research/development split</span><span>Same criteria</span><span>Same criteria â€” converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Revaluation model</span><span>NOT permitted</span><span>Permitted (rarely used) where an active market exists</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Land use rights</span><span>Classified as intangible assets</span><span>No direct equivalent construct</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">The RESEARCH/development FRAMEWORK is genuinely CONVERGED â€” the DISTINCTIVE features are the ABSENCE of a REVALUATION option (consistent with the OTHER ASBE asset standards) and the LAND use RIGHTS classification REFLECTING China's OWN land tenure SYSTEM.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every intangible asset event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Research expenditure</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Expensed as incurred</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Development expenditure (if criteria met)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Capitalised, amortised once the asset is ready for use</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 3</span><span>Investment Property â€” governs land use rights held for leasing out or capital appreciation, outside this Standard's scope</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 8</span><span>Impairment of Assets â€” governs the no-reversal impairment framework applicable to intangible assets</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Land use right (åœŸåœ°ä½¿ç”¨æƒ)</div><div class="glossary-def">A contractual right to use state- or collectively-owned land for a defined term, classified as an intangible asset when held for the enterprise's own operational use.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Development phase</div><div class="glossary-def">The stage of an internal project applying research findings to a plan for producing new or improved products, where expenditure may be capitalised if strict criteria are met.</div></div>
</div>
</div>
    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe06 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>






